        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://rockwellnc.gov/town-history/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the Yadkin Railroad built a station in Rockwell, an ex‑slave named Edmont Lindsey was the first passenger to board.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://rockwellnc.gov/town-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Historic Rockwell Museum, housed in the former post office, preserves the town’s story with photographs, documents, and artifacts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
